SUMMARY:Pavilion XL: Celebrating the Contributions of Women in Tampa Bay
LOCATION:120 W. Gasparilla Plaza Tampa \, FL 33602 United States
DESCRIPTION:Pavilion XL is a philanthropic celebration honoring the Tampa 
 Museum of Arts innovative art education programs for our diverse community
 . At Pavilion\, Tampa Bay visionaries\, leaders\, and benefactors gather t
 o raise funds that contribute to building a stronger future for the commun
 ity through the Tampa Museum of Arts programs and educational offerings. I
 n its 40th year\, Tampa Museum of Arts beloved annual gala celebrates the 
 contributions of women who have had a meaningful impact in the Tampa Bay R
 egion\, as we continue to fulfill our mission to educate\, engage\, and in
 spire our residents and visitors. This distinguished affair raises funds a
 nd awareness of Tampa Museum of Arts commitment to make art more accessibl
 e to all\, ensuring our reach extends to every corner of our community\, p
 articularly those in need. The proceeds will further fuel the Museums dedi
 cated outreach initiatives\, designed to ignite the spark of creativity in
  everyone\, including 12\,000 K-12 students who tour the museum each year 
 as well as thousands who are able to participate in art camps\, classes\, 
 and experiences because of this funding. Join us for this grand tradition 
 and celebration of the Tampa Museum of Arts innovative art education endea
 vors that serve our diverse community. \n\nPermalink: https://www.tampa.go
 v/node/196061
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/196061
END:VEVENT
