SUMMARY:Pumpkin Smash the Silence Holiday Market
LOCATION:V.O.I.C.E.S. Against Sexual Assault 1717 S 50th St Tampa \, FL 33
 619 United States
DESCRIPTION:THE ORGANIZATIONS BEHIND THE EVENT Two missions. One shared in
 vitation: Break the silence. Pumpkin Smash the Silence Holiday Market brin
 gs together Full Range Foundation and V.O.I.C.E.S. Against Sexual Assault 
 to raise awareness of womens mental health and help make meaningful suppor
 t more accessible. For Christy Hinnant and Emma Martin\, this work is pers
 onal. Their experiences have shaped a shared commitment to helping people 
 feel heard\, understand their experiences\, and move toward lives grounded
  in connection and purpose. Christy Hinnant Founder\, Executive Director\,
  President Founding Board Member  V.O.I.C.E.S. Against Sexual Assault Chri
 sty Hinnant is an eight-year U.S. Army veteran\, sexual assault survivor\,
  advocate\, and mental health professional. After experiencing sexual assa
 ult while serving at Fort Jackson in 2005\, she navigated the lasting effe
 cts of trauma and the challenges of finding effective support. Those exper
 iences inspired her to create a place where survivors could receive compas
 sionate care and find community. Christy earned her bachelors degree in Ps
 ychology from the University of North Carolina Greensboro and her masters 
 degree in Clinical Mental Health Counseling from Southern New Hampshire Un
 iversity. In 2019\, she founded V.O.I.C.E.S. Against Sexual Assault to hel
 p survivors find their voices and receive support throughout their healing
  journeys. This fundraiser helps support a free 10-week program for V.O.I.
 C.E.S. participants. Emma Martin Vice President Co-founder  Full Range Fou
 ndation Transitional Life Trauma Coach Emma Martin brings lived experience
  as a military spouse\, a background in ministry\, and a commitment to hel
 ping service members\, veterans\, and spouses navigate personal and relati
 onship challenges. She holds a bachelors degree in Religion with a minor i
 n Ministries and Ethics from Liberty University. She is currently pursuing
  a masters degree in Clinical Mental Health Counseling and working toward 
 an International Coaching Federation credential. Through Full Range Founda
 tion\, Emma helps people understand their strengths\, values\, beliefs\, a
 nd experiences while identifying practical steps toward their goals. Her C
 hristian faith informs her commitment to compassionate care\, personal dig
 nity\, and purpose. This fundraiser helps support free mental health coach
 ing services for service members and spouses. Your participation makes a d
 ifference. Come to smash a pumpkin\, shop with purpose\, or connect with y
 our community. Together\, we can bring greater visibility to womens mental
  health and help support access to care. Free Holiday Market Admission  Pu
 mpkin Smash Tickets 30 Reserve your smashing wave (https:www.fullrangefoun
 dation.comeventspumpkin-smash-the-silence-holiday-market-womens-mental-hea
 lth-awareness-fundraiser-shop-with-purpose) \n\nPermalink: https://www.tam
 pa.gov/node/197041
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.tampa.gov/node/197041
END:VEVENT
